1️⃣9️⃣ Flow Control vs Congestion Control ⭐⭐⭐

Flow Control

Prevents a fast sender from overwhelming a slow receiver.

Sender → Receiver

Congestion Control

Prevents too much traffic from overwhelming the network.

Many Senders
      ↓
   Network

🔥 Interview favorite.


---

2️⃣0️⃣ TCP Flow Control

TCP uses the receiver's advertised window to help control how much data the sender can send before overwhelming the receiver.

Think:

> Receiver capacity problem → Flow control




---

2️⃣1️⃣ TCP Congestion Control

TCP adjusts sending behavior based on network conditions.

Important concepts:

Slow Start

Congestion Avoidance

Fast Retransmit

Fast Recovery


Think:

> Network capacity problem → Congestion control




